menuconfig TFM_PARTITION_PROOF_OF_EXECUTION
    bool "Proof of Execution"
    depends on TFM_PARTITION_INITIAL_ATTESTATION
    default n

if TFM_PARTITION_PROOF_OF_EXECUTION

config POX_ALLOW_RUNTIME_KEY_OVERRIDE
    bool "Allow runtime override of the PoX signing key"
    default n
    help
      If enabled, compiles in pox_set_signing_key(), which lets a
      caller (e.g. a test partition) replace the hardcoded PoX
      signing key at runtime with a 32-byte ECDSA P-256 private
      scalar.

      Leave this disabled in production: the only signer should be
      the key hardcoded in pox_key.c.

config POX_ALLOW_PLACEHOLDER_KEY
    bool "Allow the placeholder PoX signing key (UNSAFE)"
    default n
    depends on TFM_BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      The placeholder key shipped in pox_key.c is publicly known and
      must never be used in production. By default the build will fail
      with a hard error if the key has not been replaced.

      Enable this option ONLY for initial bring-up or CI builds where
      a real key is not yet available. It is intentionally restricted
      to debug builds (TFM_BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG) and cannot be set in
      release configurations.

      NEVER enable this on a production device.

config POX_SESSION_AUTH
    bool "PoX session authentication (verifier-signed requests)"
    default y
    help
      Two-phase protocol: the verifier signs each request transcript
      (ver | session_id | nonce | faddr) with its ECDSA P-256 private
      key, and the partition verifies it with the embedded verifier
      public key before any PoX processing.

      Enforcement rules:
        - Invalid signature -> request rejected, session ended.
        - Reused nonce      -> request rejected (bounded RAM ring).

      The partition stores no session secret (public key only) and
      needs no ITS for this feature. When enabled, requests without
      session credentials are rejected with PSA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED,
      so the NS caller must supply session_id and sess_sig obtained
      from the verifier.

config POX_NONCE_HISTORY
    int "Nonce-reuse ring size (entries)"
    default 16
    depends on POX_SESSION_AUTH
    help
      Number of entries in the bounded RAM ring of SHA-256 nonce
      digests used to reject nonce reuse within one boot ("prover's
      book"). Each entry is 32 bytes; 16 entries = 512 bytes of SRAM.
      Size it to at least the number of requests expected per boot
      window in which replay must be detected device-side. The
      verifier's book remains the authoritative replay defence.

config POX_BOOT_EPOCH
    bool "Persist a boot epoch counter (one ITS write per boot)"
    default n
    depends on POX_SESSION_AUTH
    select TFM_PARTITION_INTERNAL_TRUSTED_STORAGE
    help
      Maintains a monotonically increasing boot counter in ITS and
      includes it in the PoX token claims (POX_LABEL_BOOT_EPOCH).
      Costs exactly one small ITS write per boot - O(boots), never
      O(requests) - and closes the cross-reboot window of the RAM
      nonce ring: a verifier can reject any token whose epoch does
      not match the device's current boot.

      If enabled, add the ITS service to the dependencies list in
      tfm_proof_of_execution.yaml.

endif
